{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-kx.3.1:000060:note_appended:bob-cli-kx.3.1:f4a100e6e41125e439ab906b9f23e2a2df89f4b2978ac74f5f71d61b56c09edf","timestamp":"2026-11-13T19:47:25Z","actor":"bob-cli-kx.3.1.land","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-kx.3.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"LAND AUDIT (bob-cli-kx.3.1.land): Verified that phases 3.1.1-3.1.6 landed (bob-cli c994cfbd 59b6149a 2ddfc944 cd6aefae 01ab0767; bob-plugins b519508 e102fe2). Projection, receipts, unarchive, notify, banner, and chips match the plan contracts. No unrelated post-start commit touches Gmail. Landing fixes made: clippy deny-errors (unarchive.rs, tests/gmail_support/mod.rs); a catalog Excluded row for gmail unarchive (fixed public_leaves_are_entries_or_excluded); and the bob-mail Move-back argv bug. The old argv '-- NOTE -f json' parsed -f/json as extra operands and returned human text; it is now '-f json -- NOTE', with a pin test in gmail/cli.rs, rebuilt and deployed via the documented clean-then-dirty bob plugins sync (no -F). Gates: just check passes except the tracked bob-cli-l2 and bob-cli-kl; just docs-gen is clean; docs-check fails only on the bob-cli-il and bob-cli-jz budgets; lychee shows only bob-cli-l7; bob-plugins validate passes and npm test passes except load flakes bob-cli-ju and bob-cli-ki. Remaining work, planned as a tale: the plan's unarchive fault/fence tests (wrong writer, missing scope, partial failure, journal-append failure, stale ownership, invalid_grant, policy, identity, unsafe journal), the complete-flow tests, the reopen hint still saying restore is manual-only, the receipts acceptance matrix, and the closeout of bob-cli-kx.3.1 and then phase bob-cli-kx.3."}}
